@nalind I had  to do one change in the `fixFiles` function.  When we encounter a file that ostree does not know how to manage (as a block device) we skip the ostree deduplication for the layer.  I needed to do this to support the 0/0 character devices whiteout.

We could add support for these files later on, but first it requires some changes in the ostree golang bindings otherwise we need to handle the entire logic of pruning and recreating these files.

With the new version I've pushed the whiteout layers are handled correctly and the deleted files are not visible from the container.

