@mtrmac asked some very good questions about making parent directories world-searchable, and it appears that I'd misdiagnosed why we were seeing those errors.
The permissions problem (`EACCES`) was encountered during a `mount()` with `MS_BIND` and `MS_REC` flags attempting to recursively bind mount the container's root filesystem in place, in a process which had been started in the new mount and user namespaces, after its ID mappings had already been set in `/proc` `uid_map` and `gid_map` special files.
While making the parent directories world-searchable prevented the error, it looks like it's actually enough to ensure that the owners of those directories have IDs mapped for them in the user namespace, so I've dropped `Make directories above container mounts world-searchable` and `Add a test for relaxed permissions` from this series and replaced them with `Add LayerParentOwners()  /ContainerParentOwners()`, which a caller that wants to set up user namespaces can use to determine which other UIDs and GIDs need to be mapped into the namespace.

